    <section class="section-block">
        <div class="tag-eyebrow">How it works</div>
        <h2>How to file a Form 2290 VIN Correction online</h2>
        <p class="lead">Fix a typo on your Schedule 1 in three quick steps.</p>
        <div class="step-cards">
            <div class="step-card"><div class="step-num">1</div><h3>Log in and select the return</h3><p>Choose the 2290 return that contains the incorrect VIN from your dashboard.</p></div>
            <div class="step-card"><div class="step-num">2</div><h3>Enter the corrected VIN</h3><p>Our validator flags typos and confirms VIN format before submission.</p></div>
            <div class="step-card"><div class="step-num">3</div><h3>Receive updated Schedule 1</h3><p>The IRS issues a corrected stamped Schedule 1 within minutes.</p></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-block alt">
        <div class="tag-eyebrow">What qualifies</div>
        <h2>Common VIN correction scenarios</h2>
        <p class="lead">The IRS allows VIN corrections for these cases:</p>
        <div class="step-cards">
            <div class="step-card"><div class="step-num">1</div><h3>Transposed characters</h3><p>Two digits swapped (e.g., 1HG becomes 1GH).</p></div>
            <div class="step-card"><div class="step-num">2</div><h3>Wrong letter/number</h3><p>O vs 0 or I vs 1 confusion is common on handwritten forms.</p></div>
            <div class="step-card"><div class="step-num">3</div><h3>Missing character</h3><p>A dropped digit turns a 17-character VIN into 16 — requires correction.</p></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pg-faq">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <p>Everything truckers ask about Form 2290 VIN correction e-file online.</p>
        <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleItem(this)"><span>How do I correct a wrong VIN on my Form 2290?</span><span class="plus">+</span></div><div class="faq-answer"><p>Log in to TruckTaxPro, select the accepted return, choose "VIN Correction," enter the corrected VIN, and submit. The IRS reissues a new stamped Schedule 1 with the corrected VIN — usually within minutes.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleItem(this)"><span>Is Form 2290 VIN correction free?</span><span class="plus">+</span></div><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. TruckTaxPro offers unlimited free VIN corrections for any paid 2290 return filed on our platform. No additional HVUT is owed for a VIN correction.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleItem(this)"><span>How long does a VIN correction take?</span><span class="plus">+</span></div><div class="faq-answer"><p>Most VIN corrections are IRS-accepted within minutes. You'll receive an updated stamped Schedule 1 by email as soon as the IRS processes the amendment.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleItem(this)"><span>Can I file a VIN correction for a return I filed elsewhere?</span><span class="plus">+</span></div><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. TruckTaxPro can e-file a VIN correction even if the original 2290 was filed with another provider or by paper. A small processing fee may apply.</p></div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question" onclick="toggleItem(this)"><span>What if my VIN correction is rejected?</span><span class="plus">+</span></div><div class="faq-answer"><p>Rejections usually result from a VIN mismatch with IRS records. Our support team helps you review and re-submit at no extra cost.</p></div></div>
    </section>

